'''Tata Investment Corporation''' '''Limited''' (TICL) is a non-banking financial company involved in investing in long-term investments.<ref>{{Cite web|title=TICL:Natl India Stock Quote – Tata Investment Corp Ltd|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/TICL:IN|access-date=2020-10-12|publisher=Bloomberg|language=en}}</ref>

==Background==
Earlier named the Investment Corporation of India, the company is primarily involved in investing in long-term investments such as equity shares, debt instruments, listed and unlisted, and equity-related securities of companies in a wide range of industries. The sources of income of the Company consist of dividend, interest and profit on sale of investments.<ref>{{Cite journal|last=Choksi|first=J. D.|date=1968|title=The Investment Corporation of India Limited|journal=Economic and Political Weekly|volume=3|issue=44|pages=1702–1705|jstor=4359269|issn=0012-9976}}</ref> TICL invests in sectors such as banks, cement, chemicals and fertilizers, electricity and transmission, electrical and electronics, engineering, construction and infrastructure, fast-moving consumer goods, finance and investments, healthcare, hotels, information technology, metals and mining, motor vehicles and ancillaries, oil and natural resources, retail, textiles, transportation and logistics, and miscellaneous and diversified.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://tatainvestment.com/company-profile/|title=Company Profile – Tata Investment Corporation Limited|language=en-US|access-date=2020-01-28}}</ref>

TICL was promoted{{Clarification needed|reason=what does "promoted by" mean? Bought by?|date=May 2023}} by Tata Sons in 1937 and went public in 1959 when it became one of the few publicly held investment companies listed on the [[Bombay Stock Exchange|Mumbai Stock Exchange]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bseindia.com/stock-share-price/tata-investment-corporation-ltd/tatainvest/501301/|title=Stock Share Price {{!}} Get Quote {{!}} BSE|website=bseindia.com|access-date=2020-01-28}}</ref>

